:::: section

::::section {#summary}
## Executive Summary {#summary-heading}

The first quarter of 2026 closed with all critical controls reviewed and the
outstanding items from Q4 2025 fully resolved. Two new advisory items have been
opened against the staging environment.

:::note {type="info"}
This report is formatted for A4 portrait printing. Open the rendered HTML in a
browser and use **Cmd+P → Save as PDF** to produce a deterministic PDF file.
::: note
:::: section

::::section {#kpis}
## Key Indicators {#kpis-heading}

[Critical controls passed in Q1]{.lead}

| Indicator | Q4 2025 | Q1 2026 | Δ |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Critical controls passed | 18 / 19 | 21 / 21 | +3 |
| Mean time to remediation | 11.2 days | 6.4 days | -4.8 |
| Open advisory items | 5 | 2 | -3 |
| Documents pending review | 3 | 0 | -3 |
:::: section

::::section {#risks}
## Risk Register {#risks-heading}

| ID | Risk | Severity | Owner | Status |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| R-101 | Untrusted SVG ingestion | High | Security | Mitigated |
| R-102 | Stale signing keys | Medium | Platform | Open |
| R-103 | Mixed `lang`/`dir` rendering | Low | Localization | Resolved |
| R-104 | ZIP path traversal | High | Security | Mitigated |
| R-105 | Agent target hash drift | Medium | Knowledge Systems | Open |

:::note {type="warning"}
Items marked **Open** carry remediation deadlines tracked in the operational
ticket system. They do not block this report.
::: note
:::: section

::::section {#approvals}
## Approvals {#approvals-heading}

The signatures below are placeholders for the Signature Profile. In a packaged
NODX, `signatures/document.jws` covers the canonical AST of this document.

:::quote
This report has been reviewed and approved by the parties listed below in
accordance with the Quarterly Compliance Review procedure.
::: quote

The full signature manifest is available in `signatures/document.jws` of the
packaged version.
:::: section

::::section {#methodology}
## Appendix: Methodology {#methodology-heading}

Sample selection follows ISO 19011:2018 §6.4. Evidence collection used the
agent-driven workflow described in §22 of the NODX 0.1 Working Draft. Each
finding was double-validated with a deterministic NCP projection before
inclusion in the report.
:::: section
